# Auto-commit new specimens

When you **finish adding a new specimen** (new `src/specimens/<id>/` folder + registry line in `src/specimens/index.ts` with a real `ref: 'SPX-NNN'`), **create a git commit without waiting for the user to ask**.

This is an intentional project exception to “only commit when asked.” It applies **only** to new-specimen additions, not routine edits.

## When to commit

Do commit after all of the following:

1. Specimen folder + `entry.ts` registered in `index.ts`
2. `ref` is assigned (`SPX-NNN`, not `SPX-TODO`)
3. Verification you would normally run has passed (`npm run build`, `npm run spec:check`, and `npm run test` when practical)

## When not to auto-commit

- Edits to an **existing** specimen (unless the user asked to commit)
- Chrome, harness, taxonomy-system, or docs-only work
- Incomplete scaffolds (`SPX-TODO`, empty demo, failing checks)
- Unrelated dirty files mixed in — either leave them unstaged or ask before a mixed commit

## Commit protocol

Follow the user’s git safety rules:

- Never update git config; never `--no-verify`; never force-push; do not push unless asked
- Parallel: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5 --oneline` (match message style)
- Stage **only** the new specimen folder, the `index.ts` registry line, and files that are strictly part of that specimen add (include the Persona 5 / Persona 3 / Pokémon / Dragon Ball / iOS·macOS / Android checklist mark-off when the specimen is on that backlog — see `37_persona-catalogue`)
- Message: concise, why-focused; prefer `Add SPX-NNN <title>` (1–2 sentences max)
- Use a HEREDOC for the message; run `git status` after to confirm
- If a hook fails, fix and make a **new** commit — do not amend unless the user’s amend rules all apply
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, etc.)

## One specimen per commit

If multiple new specimens were added in one session, prefer **one commit per specimen** unless the user asked otherwise.
